{"availability":"available","full":"LuminousVar/cash-track","name":"cash-track","description":"Free N8N alternative for expense tracking. Photo to Telegram, AI parses it, lands in Google Sheets. Zero server needed.","category":"Finance","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-28T13:48:08Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:25:59Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cash-track-six.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://cash-track-six.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:19.365Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:19.365Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:19.365Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:19.365Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Personal expense tracker powered by a Telegram bot. Send a receipt photo to the bot. Vision OCR reads it, DeepSeek parses it, and the result is saved to Google Sheets and shown on a SvelteKit dashboard.","Built for a single user (or a small household). Self-hosted on Vercel, data lives in your own Google Sheet.","Most projects like this reach for Supabase, Neon, PlanetScale, or some other managed database the moment data needs to be stored. For a single-user expense tracker, that means creating accounts, managing connection strings, worrying about free tier limits, and dealing with cold start latency on every serverless invocation."],"features":["Telegram bot: send a receipt photo, get an automatic reply with parsed details (merchant, total, category, items)","Vision OCR: Google Cloud Vision extracts text from any receipt image","AI parsing: DeepSeek (deepseek-flash) structures the raw text into clean JSON","Google Sheets backend: all expenses stored in a spreadsheet you own and control","SvelteKit dashboard: remaining budget with a safe daily allowance, category breakdown, recent transactions, yearly report"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LuminousVar/cash-track/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"578c08de150